# tests/read-gate.allow — the disposition file of tests/read-gate.py (tab separated)
#   file <TAB> statement-hash <TAB> index <TAB> REASON <TAB> binding <TAB> note
# An entry names ONE occurrence: the file, the hash of the statement that holds it (whitespace-normalized outside quotes,
# first 12 hex of sha256 written 4-4-4) and its index inside that statement. It matches exactly one occurrence or it is dead.
# The REASON decides nothing by itself: the scanner checks the reason's contract against the code (see read-gate.py,
# class Contracts). An entry whose occurrence is already accepted, whose statement changed, or whose contract no longer
# holds is reported, and fails once the gate is enforcing. The note is for people.
#   D display-only value   K the literal tab   H help text from the script itself   M stdin drain
#   X terminal error formatter   V view-only read at the end of the script   C continue bound to its loop
#   P metadata test with a fail-closed recheck   O python program with pinned text (binding = hash of the program)
